{
  "dom_id": "step-e5415",
  "name": "Example: Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns",
  "problem": "Let $A$ be a $4 \\times 7$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns. Find $\\textrm{rank}(A).$",
  "worked_solution": "We know that $\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $7$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n7-3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
